{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Change 3045 patch set 1: LLM-Review +1 (2 advisories), Verified -1. Root cause (CI run 39204312561, all four pytest cells): Gerrit verify takes the workflow DEFINITION from main but checks out the change's tree (ticket ee2a), so main's unguarded `MCP model schema drift gate` step ran `python -m rebar.schemas.check_mcp_models --check` against a tree where this change deleted the module (\"No module named rebar.schemas.check_mcp_models\"). pip-audit also reported failure; reading it next. Fix, in two changes under this story: (1) a workflow-only change on main that wraps the step in the ee2a if-present guard (worktree epic-04f1-guard); (2) after it merges, rebase 3045 and push patch set 2, which still deletes the step. make verify running on (1)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792389421904451186,"uuid":"7642d66a-9c00-439d-a9c3-b6d1b87d8194"}